      <h3 style="color:var(--white);margin-top:36px;">The Commercial Flow</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>An enterprise purchases Cisco Secure AI Tokens from Cisco.</li>
        <li>The tokens entitle the enterprise to consume approved AI models.</li>
        <li>Cisco manages contracting, invoicing, billing, entitlements, packaging, and support.</li>
        <li>The enterprise selects or is routed to an approved AI model.</li>
        <li>The model runs on an approved neocloud, Cisco-enabled infrastructure, or qualified model-provider environment.</li>
        <li>Cisco measures token consumption.</li>
        <li>Usage is attributed to the relevant model builder and infrastructure provider.</li>
        <li>Cisco manages partner settlement per the agreed commercial framework.</li>
        <li>The model builder earns economics from use of its model.</li>
        <li>The neocloud earns economics from compute / capacity consumed.</li>
        <li>Cisco retains the enterprise relationship and provides security, networking, governance, observability, assurance, distribution, and support.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3 style="color:var(--white);margin-top:40px;">Role of each participant</h3>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="card"><div class="icon">🔷</div><h3>Cisco</h3><p style="font-size:13px;">Merchant of record, ecosystem orchestrator, enterprise seller, and commercial aggregator.</p><ul><li>Token sales &amp; GPL placement</li><li>Contracting, invoicing, entitlements</li><li>Usage metering &amp; token accounting</li><li>Model &amp; infrastructure routing</li><li>Partner settlement</li><li>Security, identity, data governance</li><li>Splunk observability · Galileo assurance</li><li>Support · qualification · compliance · capacity orchestration</li></ul></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="icon">🧠</div><h3>Model Builders</h3><p style="font-size:13px;">Provide models, IP, inference, agentic capability, updates, and quality commitments. Earn when tokens are consumed by their model.</p><ul><li>Access to Cisco enterprise demand</li><li>Reduced contracting / billing / procurement friction</li><li>Trusted infrastructure options</li><li>Integrated security, observability, assurance</li><li>Enterprise distribution &amp; neocloud capacity</li></ul></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="icon">⚡</div><h3>Neocloud &amp; Infrastructure</h3><p style="font-size:13px;">Provide GPU compute, hosting, storage, capacity, and operations. Earn from compute / capacity consumed via token usage.</p><ul><li>Aggregated enterprise demand</li><li>Cisco sales reach &amp; infrastructure alignment</li><li>Joint reference architectures</li><li>Enterprise-grade security &amp; observability</li><li>Model-provider demand &amp; co-sell</li></ul></div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout"><p><strong style="color:var(--white);">Positioning:</strong> a three-sided, partner-powered AI marketplace and secure consumption platform — <em>not</em> a simple resale agreement or basic revenue-share. Final economics could reflect token consumption, model usage, compute, reserved capacity, infrastructure type, model cost, performance tier, geography, service level, and security/support requirements. All mechanics remain subject to validation by finance, legal, tax, accounting, product, sales, partner, revenue-recognition, and regulatory teams. <span class="tag tag-validation">Subject to Validation</span></p></div>

      <h3 style="color:var(--white);margin-top:36px;">Illustrative Transaction <span class="tag tag-illustrative">Illustrative</span></h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>An enterprise purchases a pool of Cisco Secure AI Tokens.</li>
        <li>The enterprise selects an approved specialized AI model.</li>
        <li>The model is hosted on an approved neocloud.</li>
        <li>The enterprise submits workloads to the model.</li>
