        <h2 class="section-title">Key Open Questions</h2>
        <p class="section-subtitle">Expand each group to work through the foundational decisions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="qa-group">
        <h3>Token Design</h3>
        <details class="qa"><summary>What exactly does one Cisco Secure AI Token represent?</summary><div class="qa-body">The fundamental unit of value must be defined before pricing, packaging, or billing.</div></details>
        <details class="qa"><summary>Is the token based on compute, inference, model usage, time, or outcomes?</summary><div class="qa-body">Each option has different fairness, transparency, and settlement implications.</div></details>
        <details class="qa"><summary>How are differences between models — and between GPUs / infrastructure — normalized?</summary><div class="qa-body">Normalization is central to a portable, provider-agnostic unit.</div></details>
        <details class="qa"><summary>Can tokens move across models and providers? Do they expire? Can customers reserve capacity?</summary><div class="qa-body">Portability, expiration, and reservation rules require technical and commercial design.</div></details>
      </div>
      <div class="qa-group">
        <h3>Commercial Model</h3>
        <details class="qa"><summary>Who owns pricing?</summary><div class="qa-body">Requires alignment across BU, finance, and sales.</div></details>
        <details class="qa"><summary>How are model builders and neocloud providers compensated, and what does Cisco retain?</summary><div class="qa-body">A partner-powered settlement framework, not simple revenue share.</div></details>
        <details class="qa"><summary>How are unused capacity, discounts, and settlement frequency handled?</summary><div class="qa-body">Settlement calculation and payment cadence to be defined per partner agreement.</div></details>
      </div>
      <div class="qa-group">
        <h3>Merchant-of-Record Responsibilities</h3>
        <details class="qa"><summary>Which Cisco entity acts as merchant of record; who owns invoicing, refunds, and credits?</summary><div class="qa-body">Legal entity, invoicing, and credit ownership must be established.</div></details>
        <details class="qa"><summary>Who manages disputes, contractual liability, and usage discrepancies?</summary><div class="qa-body">Liability and discrepancy ownership need clear allocation.</div></details>
        <details class="qa"><summary>How are taxes handled and revenue recognized?</summary><div class="qa-body">Tax and revenue-recognition treatment requires finance/legal validation.</div></details>
      </div>
      <div class="qa-group">
        <h3>Technical Model</h3>
        <details class="qa"><summary>Who operates token metering; how are workloads routed and model versions managed?</summary><div class="qa-body">Metering ownership and routing logic are core architecture decisions.</div></details>
        <details class="qa"><summary>How are failover, capacity reservation, data isolation, reconciliation, and portability handled?</summary><div class="qa-body">Operational resilience and data isolation must be designed and tested.</div></details>
      </div>
      <div class="qa-group">
        <h3>Security &amp; Governance</h3>
        <details class="qa"><summary>What minimum security requirements apply, and what data can models retain?</summary><div class="qa-body">Baseline security bar and data-retention rules to be defined.</div></details>
        <details class="qa"><summary>How are identity/access enforced, regulated workloads handled, and models/neoclouds approved?</summary><div class="qa-body">Approval, enforcement, and violation-handling processes required.</div></details>
      </div>
      <div class="qa-group">
        <h3>Sales &amp; GPL</h3>
        <details class="qa"><summary>What appears on GPL — one SKU or multiple? How do tiers map to SKUs?</summary><div class="qa-body">SKU structure and tier mapping to be defined with commercial teams.</div></details>
        <details class="qa"><summary>How do channel compensation, renewals, and capacity commitments work; which teams own the motion?</summary><div class="qa-body">Sales ownership and comp mechanics need alignment.</div></details>
      </div>
      <div class="qa-group">
        <h3>Support</h3>
        <details class="qa"><summary>Who owns the customer-support experience, and how are incidents divided?</summary><div class="qa-body">Support ownership across Cisco, model builders, and neoclouds must be clear.</div></details>
        <details class="qa"><summary>What support levels belong in each tier; who owns model-quality vs. infrastructure-outage issues?</summary><div class="qa-body">Tier-based support and issue ownership to be defined.</div></details>
      </div>
